{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1008938-why-are-satyrs-the-sexual-kith","id":1008938,"title":"Why are Satyrs the sexual kith?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-27T09:07:36-08:00","id":1008938,"title":"Why are Satyrs the sexual kith?","content":"Hey guys,i've been rereading changeling 2ed and i can't for the life of me understand it. Why are the satyrs considered the most sexually active kith? y'know, the <i>goatpeople </i>. It really boggles my mind and kinda breakss my suspension of disbelief. How come a person with goat's legs can be sexy? how is that even a thing??? does any of the two first editions of the books explains it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T09:17:44-08:00","id":1008942,"title":"","content":"In myth, satyrs were incredibly lusty and often depicted with permanent, enormous erections. They were often followers of Dionysus, god of revelry, and acted just the way you'd expect.<br /> <br /> Also, &quot;who come a person with goat legs can be sexy?&quot; falls apart when you consider that quite literally thousands of furries have been doing their thing for decades now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T09:18:46-08:00","id":1008943,"title":"","content":"It's actually part of the mythology on Satyrs in generally. For reasons I'm not entirely sure goats have a strong connection with lust in a few mythologies. Satyrs by extension were not necessarily sexy (rule 36 though some people are into that) but just extremely lustful creatures. So you're not necessarily talking about people looking at Satyrs and thinking &quot;Holy crap that is the hottest thing I've ever seen,&quot; more that Satyrs ended up being that guy who was more than willing to try and screw anything that looked female and the proper species.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T09:19:43-08:00","id":1008944,"title":"","content":"The symbolism of associating satyrs with sex goes back to like Greek mythology and theater. Satyriasis is the word for a man experiencing uncontrollable sexual desire. They're often depicted in art as having a permanent erection. Do some googling, you'll find a <i>lot</i> of information about the connection between satyrs and sex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T09:25:09-08:00","id":1008948,"title":"","content":"I mean, i am aware that satyrs were always the sexy ones in greek myths. i'ts just hard for me to imagine them still being so sexy in a urban fantasy setting. i just can't imagine anyone actually wanting them in their bed y'know? i'm thinking i'm just small minded","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T10:07:10-08:00","id":1008955,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm missing something, but it's not like a changeling is always going to appear in their changeling form. I mean it doesn't matter if in actuality a person is goat man, if the outward shell is human then that wouldn't throw off most people. Of course there's also the shotgun method wherein one might go after dozens upon dozens of partners and maybe only get 10% but hey that still means sex with 10 different people after you've tried 100 times.<br /> <br /> Plus this is also what Satyrs are known for. Might be that a not small amount of people are willing to overlook the goat legs for a chance to try out the reputation.<br /> <br /> Of course there's also a good hard party. Not exactly the most ethically clean, but its not exactly unheard of for one person to get wasted and make a pass at someone they wouldn't while sober and the other person to reciprocate due to lowered inhibitions. Plus if it doesn't happen you still threw a great party and had fun. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T10:26:58-08:00","id":1008966,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, i guess can understand how it happens then. It still onds a bit senselesss but alsso possiblle","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T10:53:05-08:00","id":1008973,"title":"","content":"Well there's also other Satyrs if that helps. I mean if anyone is unlikely to be uncomfortable having sex with someone who's part goat its a person who is part goat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T18:00:01-08:00","id":1009099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1008938-why-are-satyrs-the-sexual-kith?p=1008942#post1008942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, &quot;who come a person with goat legs can be sexy?&quot; falls apart when you consider that quite literally thousands of furries have been doing their thing for decades now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then again, not everyone is a Furry though...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T01:02:04-08:00","id":1009228,"title":"","content":"We also need to consider the fact that none of the changelings looks like a &quot;normal&quot; human, either. Redcaps have vicious teeth. Trolls are blue. Pooka have random animal features. Sidhe might be gorgeous, but they can also prove untouchable for many commoners. Humans usually don't see the fae mien, and changelings are used to having everyone look a little strange. Satyrs may have hairy legs, but they're also usually passionate and adventurous, and they're generally ready and willing as well. They're the original party animals, and they lower inhibitions in others wherever they go. They pursue their current passion with single-minded determination, which may very well verge on borderline worship of a potential lover. The passion they feel can't be stressed enough. Sidhe lovers may be sought for their beauty and power, but satyrs are sought out for their fiery passions and rugged primal allure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T01:09:36-08:00","id":1009230,"title":"","content":"Mythologically they were epic horndogs. And once you allowed female satyrs then yeah orgy city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T01:40:52-08:00","id":1009236,"title":"","content":"Now, the real question is why aren't most Changelings Satyrs? If you assume normal fertility, random unprotected sex results in pregnancy 2.5% of the time. 50% of the children born to Changeling-Changeling pairings and 20% of the children born to Changeling-Mortal pairings are Changeling (the rest are Kinain. Considering that the average Satyr is likely getting it on four times as much as the average Boggun, Satyrs should probably be four times as common as a Boggun. They are probably getting it on four times as much as anyone else as well, as they are a) not ugly and b) not picky. Even with protection, a male Satyr is probably plowing through enough mortal women in a year to have one Changeling child and four Kinain children every other year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T11:29:27-08:00","id":1009409,"title":"","content":"Changelings are fae souls born into human bodies, so there's no guarantee that a changeling child will necessarily be the same kith as the parent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T07:32:04-08:00","id":1009777,"title":"","content":"Short answer? Magic. <hr /><br /> Longer answer.<br /> <br /> Despite how they look what's important in this how they can make you <i>feel</i>. And satyrs are very sensual, energetic, laidback and life-appreaciating creatures.<br /> <br /> They should give you this &quot;wise magical surfer dude&quot; vibe. In the world created by 90s World of Darkness, as presented in Changling, world of constant worries, anxieties, duties and responsibilities, Satyrs in general, as an idea, represent and outlet, an escape from chains of societal norms and expectations.<br /> <br /> That is just how they think. Add their party magic, that lowers your Banality under floor and make you feel as vibrant, as you were in your youth. Free and immortal and... You get the idea. It's like a <i>magical dru</i>^W Ghrm... I mean, a breath of fresh air from beyond this rotten, poisoned and hopeless world. Because WoD is a world, where Weaver gone mad, then drove Wyrm into insanity, and Wyld now (like big letters Chaos, Madness and Dynamism force) is sanest and most helpful of all Three. And Dreaming is pure Wyld.<br /> <br /> That kind of charm might work for certain Sidhe, many commoners, mortals (who know shit) and even enchanted (if they're into that). And when it doesn't work, well, one can just be <i>around</i> Satyr and feel better and find herself suitable partner to have all fun they want. Don't think of Satyrs as succubi or vamps - they're more of <u>enablers</u> - they tend help to open up wild and carnal side of others and what others will do while at it - up to them. (Or they mess things up badly, b/c Rule of Tragedy applies.)<br /> <br /> For those reasons, it doesn't really matter, whether they have goat legs or not. And there also are Satyrs who by themselves are magically seductive (it's a Merit in their kithbook). Not all Satyrs are masters of charm and seduction, heck not all of them even care that much about being flirtatious and sexual, but they certainly have some advantages.<br /> <br /> P.S. But essentially, yeah, Sidhe are the real perverts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":5211,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","user":"Firkraag","date":". 11-29-2016, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T10:46:51-08:00","id":1009860,"title":"","content":"Are Changeling souls limited in number? I do not think they have ever set a firm cap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T14:14:37-08:00","id":1009934,"title":"","content":"The fae souls in necessarily finite but it doesn't mean the number is low. I think there is a lot of changeling souls a large part of them not even being incarnate yet (some are in Arcadia, some others are on the Bright Road).<br /> <br /> For the OP, like some said before, don't forget that Satyr have a power that lowers your Banality and lifts your inhibitions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T17:06:24-08:00","id":1010409,"title":"","content":"I would think that fae souls are potentially infinite, at least as long as there are living humans, because they are born of human dreams and human nightmares. Concerning the genetics of Changelings, I am not sure if Changelings can be born to parents of another Kith. Otherwise, why were there no Sidhe on Earth before the 60s?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T19:28:54-08:00","id":1010460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1008938-why-are-satyrs-the-sexual-kith?p=1010409#post1010409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think that fae souls are potentially infinite, at least as long as there are living humans, because they are born of human dreams and human nightmares. Concerning the genetics of Changelings, I am not sure if Changelings can be born to parents of another Kith. Otherwise, why were there no Sidhe on Earth before the 60s?</div> </div> </div> </div>Faerie souls are immortal but not infinite. The world is all but consumed by banality, making it nearly impossible for new faerie souls to come into being. Modern changelings are the dying embers of a once proud race desperately trying to keep the spark of humanity lit in the face of overwhelming despair. Any new faerie souls to come into being during the current times would be a momentous occasion indeed. <br /> <br /> They don't reproduce sexually (except for when they do), so genetics doesn't play a part in creating a new faerie (again, except for when it does). Faerie souls seem to be more attracted to human family lines with faerie blood, so families with faerie ancestry are more likely to have changeling children. Fae of a certain kith may be more attracted to families who share their blood, but there is nothing that prevents a changeling of one kith to be born of parents descended of another.<br /> <br /> There were exceedingly few sidhe on Earth from the time of the Shattering until the late 1960s because the nobility fled to Arcadia just before the two worlds became sealed apart. Most of those who did stay behind weren't able to withstand the onslaught of banality like their commoner counterparts, and were utterly destroyed. It wasn't until the Resurgence that glamour was finally able to regain a little ground against banality, reopening the gates between the two worlds and allowing the sidhe to return to Earth and undergo some form of the Changeling Way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T14:26:11-08:00","id":1010818,"title":"","content":"As for the goat legs being a turn off, don't forget that changelings are part dream. They see a satyr and a human part of them see a half goat, half human. But the changeling soul in them see a thousand stories of passion, freedom and lust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12678-monkeydjie","name":"Monkeydjie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T08:48:33-08:00","id":1011102,"title":"","content":"And I imagine that the there are secret furries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T14:02:44-08:00","id":1011211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1008938-why-are-satyrs-the-sexual-kith?p=1011102#post1011102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I imagine that the there are secret furries.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think its more relevant for enchanted mortals than changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12678-monkeydjie","name":"Monkeydjie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T15:43:06-08:00","id":1017829,"title":"","content":"To put it in <i>Mage</i> terms:<br /> <br /> Every good mage knows that belief is power, even for the Sleepers. It is belief that makes a given spell coincidental or vulgar, belief that shapes what a mage can or can't do. And it is the awesome might of Unbelief that crushes a mystic' supernatural allies, annihilating them for the crime of existing when the Consensus says they shouldn't.<br /> <br /> What most mages never stop to wonder is whether there is a constructive counterpart to Unbelief, something that makes the impossible real. The Sleepers have Avatars, too, after all - they're just not actively shaping the universe.<br /> <br /> The Dreaming is a result of that countering phenomena - &quot;that which should exist, does&quot;. Anything enough humans actively belief in, dream about, fear . . .eventually become real (at least chimerically).<br /> <br /> So when an entire civilization is convinced there are sexually ravenous goat-men have orgies in the woods, seducing any woman who wanders by . . . Well, sooner or later, there actually <i>will</i> be sexually ravenous goat-men in those woods. . .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1008938-why-are-satyrs-the-sexual-kith?p=1008948#post1008948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, i am aware that satyrs were always the sexy ones in greek myths. i'ts just hard for me to imagine them still being so sexy in a urban fantasy setting. i just can't imagine anyone actually wanting them in their bed y'know? i'm thinking i'm just small minded</div> </div> </div> </div>In the words of <i>Austin Powers</i>. they are &quot;hairy like wild animal!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Each kith is born from a specific dream or fantasy, and satyrs <i>aren't</i> a love-type. Reciting sonnets, scattering rose petals on the bed . . . that's sidhe territory. No, satyrs are a <i>sex</i> fantasy. The dream of ripping you clothes off, and just going at it, until the bed collapses around the two of you . . . fifteen hours later.<br /> <br /> A female satyr is never &quot;too tired&quot; for sex, never &quot;has a headache&quot;. A male never has &quot;performance anxiety&quot;, nor goes soft at an inopportune time. If you want sweet and thoughtful gestures from your partner, look elsewhere. A satyr is for when you want to rut like animals in heat.<br /> <br /> They're everything a bored Greek noblewoman imagined, when she fantasized about some barbarian carrying her off and having his way with her. What every repressed medieval clergyman feared a certain hoofed-and-horned demon might convince his congregation to do. What every modern woman hopes for when she develops a crush on a &quot;fugly&quot; musician, and tries to sneak back stage.<br /> <br /> And that carries through to their kith. On some level, even mundanes recognize a satyr as a wild potential sex partner. After all, that's what the mundanes created them to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 12-15-2016, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T16:55:36-08:00","id":1033731,"title":"","content":"A quick note, the death of Euridice, wife of Orpheus, on greek mythology, were caused by a satyr.<br /> <br /> In greek mythology, they were a representative of the male impulse, the animus, a primal instinct...<br /> <br /> Well, basically, Eur\u00eddice choose death rather than being raped by this brute male primordial force.<br /> <br /> So... An unseelie satyr perhaps, translating to C:tD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T17:02:54-08:00","id":1033734,"title":"","content":"I might not be an expert on Changelings...but i know a thing or two about sensualists (Once you party with a Cultist of Ectasy you can understand Everything *Cue Rod Stewart* <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Hphwfq1wLJs\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Hphwfq1wLJs</a> )<br /> <br /> personally, i think its mainly because they are the most laid ones, the ones who can appreciate the simplest things. I belive that they like to...how to put it....live by enjoying the passion's of life and showing it by being -not constantly aroused- but enjoying the moment...<br /> <br /> The Dude Abides sort of deal. but if you can mix some kinky in there, well... all the better, after all life is to celebrate<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T21:15:27-07:00","id":1121701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1008938-why-are-satyrs-the-sexual-kith#post1008938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys,i've been rereading changeling 2ed and i can't for the life of me understand it. Why are the satyrs considered the most sexually active kith? y'know, the <i>goatpeople </i>. It really boggles my mind and kinda breakss my suspension of disbelief. How come a person with goat's legs can be sexy? how is that even a thing??? does any of the two first editions 