m/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1008938-why-are-satyrs-the-sexual-kith?p=1010409#post1010409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would think that fae souls are potentially infinite, at least as long as there are living humans, because they are born of human dreams and human nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That may have been true <i>before the shattering</i>, but things are different now. The Age of Reason has gradually weakened humanity's capacity to dream over the centuries. We're becoming more grounded in what we perceive to be reality. Our imagination is dying, and the fae are dying with it; that's the horror that surrounds the game. We're facing a slow, inevitable decline into a boring, repetitive world of hard science and secular logic.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the souls being infinite, I believe the fae are supposed to be immortal. As long as they are not Undone by the effects of Banality, their spirits can reincarnate into new bodies when their previous one dies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}